---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site";
---

<Legal title="Privacy Policy" description={`What ${SITE.name} does and does not do with visitors' information.`}>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is a personal blog. It is built to collect as little about visitors as possible.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It has no accounts, comments, forms or newsletter sign-up, so it asks you for no personal details.</li>
    <li>It uses no advertising, tracking pixels or analytics scripts, and sets no cookies.</li>
    <li>It loads no fonts, scripts or images from other companies' servers. Fonts and search run from this site.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is kept in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    If you choose Light or Dark with the theme switch, that choice is saved in your browser's local storage under
    the name "theme", so the site looks the same next time. It never leaves your device and can be cleared in your
    browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Search</h2>
  <p>
    Search works inside your browser, using an index of the posts that is downloaded in small pieces as you type.
    Your search words are not sent to anyone and are not stored.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Like any website, the company that hosts this site may keep technical records of requests, such as the IP address,
    the page requested and the time, for security and operation. The author does not receive or use these records
    to identify visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Posts may link to other websites. Those sites have their own privacy practices, which are not covered here.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this changes, for instance if analytics or comments are added, this page will be updated and the date at the
    top revised.
  </p>
</Legal>
